/E (Currently, food donation and redistribution efforts mostly rely on manual processes, disconnected communication channels, and paper-based record keeping. Donors interested in sharing surplus food typically have limited access to coordinated platforms, making it difficult to efficiently inform organizations or delivery personnel. Administrators face challenges in tracking donation requests, verifying food availability, and managing logistics without real-time data. Delivery agents often lack systematic approaches for organizing pickups and drop-offs, leading to delays and wastage.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
